    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded at Ava by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nyaungyan-min">Nyaungyan Min</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayinnaung">Bayinnaung</a>, after the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-toungoo-empire">First Toungoo Empire</a> in 1599.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anaukpetlun">Anaukpetlun</a> took Syriam from the Portuguese in 1613; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thalun">Thalun</a> moved the capital back to Ava and ordered a revenue inquest.</li><li>Weakened by Manipuri raids and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mon-people">Mon</a> rising in 1740, it fell when southern forces took Ava in 1752.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Portuguese captives taken at Syriam in 1613 were resettled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-burma">Upper Burma</a> as royal gunners; their Catholic descendants, the bayingyi, still live in villages there.</p></aside>
    </section>

